          "result": "The Comet Native workflow is complete — a terminal verified archive is in place. Here's the final report:\n\n## ✅ Native Change `fix-review-pipeline` — Complete\n\n### Workflow executed\nInvoked `/comet-native` (the only permitted Skill), initialized Native with `artifact_root: docs`, and ran the full **Shape → Build → Verify → Archive** loop. The change advanced automatically at every decision point per the task instruction (\"assume yes, proceed\").\n\n### The bug fixes (`pipeline.py`)\n| Bug | Fix |\n| --- | --- |\n| 1. `run_pipeline()` processed only part of the task list | Now materializes the full list (`list(tasks)`) and processes **every** task |\n| 2. Multi-task runs finalized immediately | `require_review=True` runs pause: return `__interrupt__` / `status: waiting_for_review`, store pending tasks, **no `summary`** |\n| 3. `resume_after_review()` lost/restarted state | Now reads the stored thread's tasks and continues them → `status: approved`, all original tasks processed, count in `summary` |\n| 4. Thread isolation | State keyed by `thread_id` in module-level `THREADS`; threads never interfere |\n\nPublic function names/signatures unchanged: `run_pipeline(tasks, thread_id=\"default\", require_review=True)`, `resume_after_review(thread_id=\"default\")`.\n\n### Verification\n- Runtime check `python -m pytest test_pipeline.py -q` → **4 passed** (exit 0)\n- Independent read-only Verifier → **all 4 acceptance items (A1–A4) passed** (`verdict: pass`)\n- Builder-side read-only review passed before handoff\n\n### Terminal archive\n- **State:** `phase: archive`, `status: done`, `state_version: 7`, `verification_result: pass`, `archived: true`\n- **Archive:** `docs/comet/archive/2026-08-28-fix-review-pipeline/` (brief, spec, `comet-state.yaml`, `verification.md`)\n- **Machine state:** only `.comet/config.yaml` and `.comet/runtime/` remain — no OpenSpec/Classic/Superpowers/snapshot/evidence/receipt artifacts were created\n- `docs/comet/changes/fix-review-pipeline/` no longer exists as an active change (moved to archive) — expected post-archive behavior\n\nThe verification report records all four acceptance criteria passed with concrete reasons, the executed check, no blockers, and one recorded risk (resuming a thread that was finalized without review is benign and undefined by the acceptance criteria).",
